//@version=3
study("UCTPROBE_VW_HLINE_DEFAULTS_V3", overlay = false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-22 (Q-HLINE-3, docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-11-22-e96-presentation.md). Our probe.
// NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW.
//
// ─── TRADINGVIEW'S OWN DEFAULTS FOR A v5 `hline`, ONE FIELD AT A TIME ───
//
// v1-v3 line style (dashed) and width (1) are captured (S1, transparency-defaults-by-version-rddt-1d-2026-11-14),
// and the v6 defaults (vw-hline-written). The v3 default COLOUR is not. Only the v6 defaults are captured (`vw-hline-written-rddt-1d-2026-11-20`, H5: #808080, dashed, width 1). Until
// these rows are, a v3 hline that names no colour, style or width is drawn in the chart's neutral ink and named
// (`app/src/components/chart/engine/hlineLevels.js::HLINE_DEFAULTS`). Each row leaves exactly one field unwritten.
//
//   P0  close (a plot, so the pane has a scale)
//   D0  price 100, nothing else                       (colour, style and width all TradingView's)
//   D1  price 110, colour and width written           (the default STYLE)
//   D2  price 120, colour and style written           (the default WIDTH)
//   D3  price 130, style and width written            (the default COLOUR)
//   D4  price 140, red written                  (a palette colour kept opaque, or not)
// CAPTURE: NYSE:RDDT 1D from the listing, inputs at defaults; record study.bands / bandDefaults / bandState.

plot(close, title = "P0_close", color = gray)
hline(100, title = "D0_nothing")
hline(110, title = "D1_default_style", color = blue, linewidth = 2)
hline(120, title = "D2_default_width", color = green, linestyle = dotted)
hline(130, title = "D3_default_colour", linestyle = solid, linewidth = 3)
hline(140, title = "D4_red_only", color = red)
